cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Linear Structural Dynamics"
# STAGE 2 ONLY (after the Zenodo release): add the concept DOI on the next line.
# doi: {{CONCEPT_DOI}}
abstract: >-
  A coding-first book on linear structural dynamics with NumPy and OpenSeesPy, built
  around one numerical solver for the equation of motion that is handed every kind of
  load. The solver is applied to free vibration, harmonic and periodic loads, arbitrary
  loads and earthquakes, and then to yielding oscillators, modal analysis of multi-story
  buildings, and response-spectrum analysis and the equivalent lateral force method of
  ASCE 7. Every chapter combines worked examples, diagrams and interactive figures, and
  its code cells can be run in the browser.
authors:
  - family-names: Talebi-Kalaleh
    given-names: Mohammad
    affiliation: University of Alberta
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3754-5992"
